  "label": "political_disinformation_consumers",
  "description": "The meme is designed for audiences who are susceptible to or actively seek out political disinformation. The false claims about Clinton’s actions (deleting 34,000 emails, using WeChat, destroying phones) are presented as factual, appealing to individuals who may not critically evaluate the accuracy of the information. The meme’s structure—using visual cues (Clinton speaking at a podium) and accusatory text—reinforces the false narrative, making it effective for audiences who are more likely to accept sensationalized claims without verification.",
